      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think they need to restrict Veteran level to people that had accounts created before a certain date in 2017 on top of the other requirements. Other then that the ranking system is doing OK but could be tweaked to stop crashers from ranking up",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-22T07:16:49.429Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Despite wanting to reach veteran rank to show off, I think it would be fine just to have something as simple as a good and bad category. It would work similarly to the credit system irl. New players starts somewhere on the lower end of the good category. Trust would increase over time when mingling with the general public and consecutive blocks/kicks/violations can drastically decrease it.. Of course vrchat would have to flesh out the specific variables. \nMain reason to do without the various ranks is to reduce discrimination; especially against newer players who have yet to do any wrong. They should still be unable to create content until reaching a certain point, but at least they will not outright be treated 'less fairly' than veteran or higher rank players. Oh, and all the different color name tags would be horrible. I personally think that the name tag should be the least conspicuous part of a player.",
